{"uid":"eb90e418b67bce28","name":"test_two_drains_racing_on_the_same_row_cannot_both_win","fullName":"tests.test_calibration_jobs#test_two_drains_racing_on_the_same_row_cannot_both_win","historyId":"e4bdb7f1b4c2f2f0b7c89110c7c12873","time":{"start":1786397332745,"stop":1786397332768,"duration":23},"description":"The conditional UPDATE is the real arbitration, exercised through the real function.\n\n    Two weaker versions of this test were written first and both proved nothing. Calling\n    ``claim_next_job`` twice in sequence is useless because the second drain's ``SELECT``\n    already excludes the row. Issuing the ``UPDATE`` directly from the test is worse: it\n    hardcodes the predicate in the test, so it passes even when production stops using one.\n    Both survived deleting the ``status`` predicate from ``claim_next_job``.\n\n    The dangerous interleaving is both drains selecting the same queued row *before* either\n    updates it. This reproduces it by letting a competitor claim the row in the window\n    between this drain's SELECT and its UPDATE, then asserting this drain comes away with\n    nothing. It fails if the predicate is removed.\n\n    It matters because calibration invokes tools, so running one job twice is not a\n    harmless duplicate.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The conditional UPDATE is the real arbitration, exercised through the real function.</p>\n<pre><code>Two weaker versions of this test were written first and both proved nothing. Calling\n``claim_next_job`` twice in sequence is useless because the second drain's ``SELECT``\nalready excludes the row. Issuing the ``UPDATE`` directly from the test is worse: it\nhardcodes the predicate in the test, so it passes even when production stops using one.\nBoth survived deleting the ``status`` predicate from ``claim_next_job``.\n\nThe dangerous interleaving is both drains selecting the same queued row *before* either\nupdates it. This reproduces it by letting a competitor claim the row in the window\nbetween this drain's SELECT and its UPDATE, then asserting this drain comes away with\nnothing. It fails if the predicate is removed.\n\nIt matters because calibration invokes tools, so running one job twice is not a\nharmless duplicate.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1786397247521,"stop":1786397247521,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1786397252834,"stop":1786397252834,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_default_tests_to_trusted_header_auth","time":{"start":1786397332347,"stop":1786397332347,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1786397332347,"stop":1786397332347,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_clear_prompt_info_cache","time":{"start":1786397332347,"stop":1786397332347,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_reset_pricing_source","time":{"start":1786397332348,"stop":1786397332348,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachment